{"call_id": "71ab646c3d2d4c98a0e46c879c386df5", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/fullbench/runs/natural/stockindex/query3/full-01/results/71ab646c3d2d4c98a0e46c879c386df5.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"TASK: If an investor had made regular monthly investments in all indices since 2000, which 5 indices would have produced the highest overall returns, and what countries do they belong to?\\n\\nMETHODOLOGY:\\n- Used indextrade_database (DuckDB) daily prices, CloseUSD (USD-converted closes) for cross-country comparability.\\n- Simulated dollar-cost averaging: invest $1 at the first trading day of every month from January 2000 (or the index's first available date after 2000) through each index's last available date (~May/June 2021), accumulating units.\\n- Overall return = (final portfolio value - total invested) / total invested.\\n- Countries determined by matching each index symbol to its exchange in indexinfo_database (index_info table).\\n\\nRESULTS - TOP 5 INDICES BY OVERALL RETURN:\\n\\n1. IXIC (NASDAQ Composite) — United States (NASDAQ)\\n   Return: +382.7% ($257 invested monthly Jan 2000–May 2021 grew to $1,240.52)\\n\\n2. NSEI (NIFTY 50) — India (National Stock Exchange of India)\\n   Return: +135.8% ($165 invested monthly Sep 2007–May 2021 grew to $389.14)\\n\\n3. 399001.SZ (Shenzhen Component) — China (Shenzhen Stock Exchange)\\n   Return: +134.7% ($258 invested grew to $605.65)\\n\\n4. GDAXI (DAX) — Germany (Frankfurt Stock Exchange)\\n   Return: +134.7% ($257 invested grew to $603.19)\\n\\n5. TWII (Taiwan Weighted) — Taiwan (Taiwan Stock Exchange)\\n   Return: +129.8% ($257 invested grew to $590.64)\\n\\nFor reference, the remaining indices ranked: N225 (Japan) +116.9%, NYA (United States) +101.5%, GSPTSE (Canada) +73.0%, 000001.SS (China) +64.3%, N100 (Euronext/pan-Europe) +61.3%, HSI (Hong Kong) +60.5%, SSMI (Switzerland) +58.8%, J203.JO (South Africa) +37.5%.\\n\\nNOTE: Some indices have data starting after 2000 (NSEI from Sep 2007, J203.JO from Feb 2012); for those, monthly investments began at their first available date. The NASDAQ Composite (US) is the clear winner; the remaining top-5 order (India, China-Shenzhen, Germany, Taiwan) is robust because their returns cluster well above the rest.\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
